{"id":"478084993","kind":"article","title":"助记媒介可能会促使读者更缓慢、更专心地阅读","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7W1Zr7wEGptA3bFYwwaPbCFLBo54xXmQLQdK"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"助记媒介 & 思想工具","date":"2022-03-10","updated":"2024-01-25","votes":10,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":768,"keywords":["助记媒介","阅读理解","嵌入式问题","阅读注意力","元认知"],"summary":"作者记录《量子国度》读者的访谈反馈：穿插在阅读中的问题卡可能让人放慢速度、留意走神；他推测，这种效果或能促进文本加工与理解，不只帮助记忆。文章把这一解释作为假说，并提出比较有无嵌入问题的阅读时间，排除思考问题的时间后再观察，或结合眼动数据检验。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/478084993","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"WTTyDykD\">《<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2fBHADWa93EZTuNzuww7V3Vi587ZyZ4FHTHm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">量子国度</a>》的读者在采访中用不同方式告诉我们，嵌入的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSoTbuyrXFnDHibaSeEzPRx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">附加问题</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zE1sr3TTDoEJut4hgai2w6qFUwBYHSkk7no\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>）促使他们更仔细地阅读，或帮助他们注意到走神的情况。撇开卡片对记忆的直接影响不谈，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4rRX3qwSSJRsEkdXKwH2shamgHNeRthrMLiF\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>中添加的问题，可能只是帮助读者在阅读时放慢脚步，并专注于所读内容。<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zX1WtJ4ouE8sjN1NgWHsGVg8ZnVfp5Kz74Vs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">理解概念需与其尽力较量</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>，所以助记媒介的这种效果可能会让读者理解更深刻。或者更简单地说，它可以促进基本的阅读理解（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z59PYkSdPeznr95fco4GRQx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">人们经常难以回忆起文本的细节，原因在于他们起初就根本没有加工文本</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>）。</p><p data-pid=\"qkYoguuW\">复习区还让阅读自然地停顿，有点类似于 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zxRE7XavvhxgY3EkFduYB5B4fnMBknizq52u\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Eckhart Tolle 的停顿符号</a>，但复习区不比停顿符号具有反思性。相关的：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4sXBJLQQrFYFUKPE9nrW5gDndYWCPP7Kic\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介复习集使阅读过程产生了自然的中断</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup></p><p data-pid=\"Hm-srP5t\">对于同一篇文章，比较嵌入问题的版本，和没有嵌入问题的版本的阅读时间，估计会很有趣。嵌入问题版本的阅读时间需要排除思考问题的时间。应用上眼球追踪数据也许很有用。</p><p data-pid=\"Sl2WcpcB\">相关笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2T1wfESQC8moFh2Er4pHkHxkm3SoSzVvBsEo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">大多数解释型媒体对参与者提出了沉重的元认知要求</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"qFYA_Dn_\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"679063443\" href=\"#/post/679063443\">阅读理解</a></li><li data-pid=\"tnIXM90c\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"459483765\" href=\"#/post/459483765\">助记媒介 (Mnemonic medium)</a></li><li data-pid=\"7ZJT5b-G\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"463608296\" href=\"#/post/463608296\">助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中</a></li><li data-pid=\"v67dKLyh\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"599394904\" href=\"#/post/599394904\">将助记媒介应用于非技术性文章的经验教训</a></li><li data-pid=\"duiEiqOs\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"638575907\" href=\"#/post/638575907\">将助记媒介看作更深入理解文本的手段会怎么样？</a></li><li data-pid=\"cQiPF_1b\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677786021\" href=\"#/post/677786021\">附加问题能够提高学习者对相关但未直接测试的内容的理解</a></li><li data-pid=\"nbmkTKFG\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677786105\" href=\"#/post/677786105\">人们经常难以回忆起文本的细节，原因在于他们起初就根本没有加工文本</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"EXe-X8pe\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"YNDYWdse\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7W1Zr7wEGptA3bFYwwaPbCFLBo54xXmQLQdK\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The mnemonic medium may push readers to read more slowly and attentively (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 附加问题 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677785901\" href=\"#/post/677785901\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"463608296\" href=\"#/post/463608296\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 助记媒介 (Mnemonic medium) <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"459483765\" href=\"#/post/459483765\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 理解概念需与其尽力较量 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"442692019\" href=\"#/post/442692019\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 人们经常难以回忆起文本的细节，原因在于他们起初就根本没有加工文本 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"677786105\" href=\"#/post/677786105\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 助记媒介的复习集使阅读过程产生了自然的中断 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"542688360\" href=\"#/post/542688360\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 大多数解释型媒体对参与者提出了沉重的元认知要求 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"476696005\" href=\"#/post/476696005\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"476588071","title":"情景体验需要参与者置身的因果关系","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":12,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"481230325","title":"助记媒介应该允许读者对他们收集的卡片进行控制","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":9,"minutes":5,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 助记媒介 & 思想工具"},{"id":"677786105","title":"人们经常难以回忆起文本的细节，原因在于他们起初就根本没有加工文本","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":39,"minutes":4,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"463608296","title":"助记媒介卡片穿插在阅读过程中","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":6,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"542688360","title":"助记媒介的复习集使阅读过程产生了自然的中断","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":8,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"643871124","title":"Andy Matuschak - 自学，间隔重复，以及为什么书本不起作用","author":"Dwarkesh Patel","votes":289,"minutes":95,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「元认知」· Dwarkesh Patel"}],"rec_answers":[]}